{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1465890-question-with-knack-and-boon","id":1465890,"title":"question with knack and boon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-30T06:00:39-07:00","id":1465890,"title":"question with knack and boon","content":"Hello,<br /> I have questions with some knacks and boons:<br /> Calling Guargian =&gt; A Talisman : grants the bearer 2 Enhancement to rolls made to defend.<br /> So if the player made a roll defense with 1 success, his defense is 4 aka 1 standard + 1 success +2 from the knack? If not when use it?<br /> <br /> Purview Heath =&gt; Innate Power : Gain enhancement 1 on Stamina rolls.<br /> So if the player made a roll defense with 1 success, his defense is 3 aka 1 standard + 1 success +1 from the innate power?<br /> <br /> Purview Sun =&gt; Penetrating Glare : Add Enhancement 3 on any rolls to determine whether a character is lying etc..<br /> Why enhancement? If the difficulty is 3, how enhancement can help if the player roll 2 success? How the boon can help?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your response<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26485-mk3ultimate","name":"mk3ultimate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T11:34:27-07:00","id":1465930,"title":"","content":"I think it would actually be a defense of 3. My reading of the standard defense action is that your default defense is 1 and no matter how bad the defense roll gets or other penalties are your defense can't drop below 1. The defense action can raise it, but if you only got 1 success (I'm ignoring other factors for the moment) then what you've done is matched standard, but if you rolled 2 successes then your defense would be 2 ignoring anything else. Now in this case the knack is still useful because even if you only got 1 success enhancement 2 means you still come out of it with a defense of 3 that round or to use for other defensive stunts like diving for cover.<br /> <br /> As for penetrating glare, remember enhancements apply on the caveat that you rolled successes not that you succeeded on the roll. So your scenario of trying to see through a lie with a difficulty of 3 and only rolling two successes means adding penetrating glare to the equation gives you a total of five successes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T01:36:24-08:00","id":1467026,"title":"","content":"Ok il's clear now! Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26485-mk3ultimate","name":"mk3ultimate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}